# Local development environment template.
#
# You usually do NOT need a .env file locally. `bun run dev` works with zero
# configuration: it defaults to SQLite at .tmp/dev.db and skips Docker entirely.
#
# Copy this file to .env (or export the variables in your shell) ONLY if you
# want to override the defaults below.

PORT=3001

# Comma-separated CIDRs for reverse proxies whose X-Forwarded-For header may
# be trusted. Leave empty for direct/local development.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: SQLite at .tmp/dev.db (no Docker, no Postgres process).
# Set DATABASE_URL only if you want to use Postgres or a custom SQLite path.
#
#   SQLite (file):    DATABASE_URL=sqlite:./path/to/your.db
#   SQLite (memory):  DATABASE_URL=sqlite::memory:
#   Postgres (auto):  DATABASE_URL=postgres://studio:studio@127.0.0.1:5433/studio
#                     (`bun run dev` will start the Docker postgres service automatically)
#
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:./.tmp/dev.db

# ─── Filesystem paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
UPLOADS_DIR=./uploads
STATIC_DIR=./dist

# ─── AI credential encryption ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev auto-creates .tmp/secret.key. Production deployments must set
# STUDIO_SECRET_KEY to the output of:
#
#   bun run scripts/generate-secret-key.ts
#
# STUDIO_SECRET_KEY=

# ─── Claude Code (subscription) provider on macOS ───────────────────────────
# The `claude` CLI keeps its credentials in the macOS Keychain, which
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR cannot relocate. On a Mac serving SEVERAL Studio users
# they would all silently share one Claude login, so the provider is disabled
# on macOS by default.
#
# On a single-user development machine there is no second user to leak a login
# to. Set this to 1 to enable the provider there. Leave it unset on any host
# more than one person can reach — it asserts "I am the only user", it does
# not fix the Keychain.
#
# STUDIO_ALLOW_MACOS_CLAUDE_CLI=1

# Let the agent fetch assets served on LOOPBACK. The concrete case is the Figma
# Dev Mode MCP server (127.0.0.1:3845), whose get_design_context returns asset
# download URLs on http://localhost:3845/assets/... — the SSRF guard blocks
# those by default, which is why an agent reports it cannot download icons or
# images.
#
# The trade is real: with this on, any URL the agent supplies can reach any
# service on this host, including Studio's own API. Loopback only — RFC1918,
# CGNAT and link-local (cloud metadata) stay blocked either way.
#
# Set it only on a single-user development machine. Leave it unset on any host
# more than one person can reach.
#
# STUDIO_ALLOW_LOOPBACK_ASSET_FETCH=1
